WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.020
Meet the Korok family.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.700
Two men and their three foster children.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.720
Until now, adopting children hasn't been an
option for the gay couple.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:15.210
In Germany, same-sex partnerships don't yet
have the same legal status as married couples.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:21.220
"Our wish is for our union to no longer be
seen as a second-class marriage.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.589
Not just to be registered life partners - but
to have a fully recognised, normal marriage-

00:00:26.589 --> 00:00:33.900
where we have the exact same marital status
as everyone else.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.130
If the German parliament votes yes on the
so-called "Marriage for Everyone" law, the

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:40.240
couple would be allowed to adopt.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.000
They say that would be a win-win situation
for both them and their children.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.550
"The opportunity to adopt children as your
own helps secure their financial future, as

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.870
it would with your own children.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.710
Think about all the things that go with adoption.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:02.770
Child custody is in the here and now -- but
adoption is connected to inheritance - future

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:07.289
financial security for the children."

00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:09.259
Both men have campaigned for gender equality

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:10.479
for years.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:14.860
But they say they're not grateful to German
Chancellor Angela Merkel for her sudden policy

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.100
turn around on gay marriage.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:29.259
"What is being voted on is something we think
is self-evident.

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:31.340
It should've happened a long time ago.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:36.600
I'll be happy if the bill passes, but in the
end, it's like getting something you feel

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.539
you've been entitled to for a long time."

00:01:40.539 --> 00:01:45.610
In the future, Michael and Kai Korok hope
that the difference between homosexual and

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:51.189
heterosexual couples will disappear completely
– both from law books – and from the way

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:53.740
people think about relationships.

